{"id":"e54dcda1-24de-4d7e-8aa7-55586d31fb8c","object":"chat.completion","created":1785002150,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    import itertools\\n    lengths = case['lengths']\\n    scores = case['scores']\\n    budget = case['budget']\\n    n = len(lengths)\\n    # brute force for small n, DP for larger\\n    if n <= 20:\\n        best_score = float('-inf')\\n        best_tokens = 0\\n        best_indices = []\\n        for mask in range(1 << n):\\n            total_len = 0\\n            total_score = 0.0\\n            indices = []\\n            for i in range(n):\\n                if mask & (1 << i):\\n                    total_len += lengths[i]\\n                    total_score += scores[i]\\n                    indices.append(i)\\n            if total_len <= budget:\\n                # compare: higher score, then fewer tokens, then lexicographic indices\\n                if (total_score > best_score or\\n                    (total_score == best_score and total_len < best_tokens) or\\n                    (total_score == best_score and total_len == best_tokens and indices < best_indices)):\\n                    best_score = total_score\\n                    best_tokens = total_len\\n                    best_indices = indices\\n        return {'selected_indices': best_indices, 'tokens_used': best_tokens, 'total_score': best_score}\\n    else:\\n        # DP with dictionary, storing tuple (score, tokens_used, indices_tuple)\\n        dp = {0: (0.0, 0, ())}  # tokens -> (score, tokens_used, indices)\\n        for i, (l, s) in enumerate(zip(lengths, scores)):\\n            new_dp = dp.copy()  # exclude current item\\n            for tokens, (score, _, indices) in dp.items():\\n                new_tokens = tokens + l\\n                if new_tokens <= budget:\\n                    new_score = score + s\\n                    new_indices = indices + (i,)\\n                    existing = new_dp.get(new_tokens)\\n                    if existing is None:\\n                        new_dp[new_tokens] = (new_score, new_tokens, new_indices)\\n                    else:\\n                        old_score, old_tokens, old_indices = existing\\n                        # compare: higher score wins, then lower tokens, then lexicographic indices\\n                        if (new_score > old_score or\\n                            (new_score == old_score and new_tokens < old_tokens) or\\n                            (new_score == old_score and new_tokens == old_tokens and new_indices < old_indices)):\\n                            new_dp[new_tokens] = (new_score, new_tokens, new_indices)\\n            dp = new_dp\\n        best_score = float('-inf')\\n        best_tokens = 0\\n        best_indices = ()\\n        for tokens, (score, _, indices) in dp.items():\\n            if (score > best_score or\\n                (score == best_score and tokens < best_tokens) or\\n                (score == best_score and tokens == best_tokens and indices < best_indices)):\\n                best_score = score\\n                best_tokens = tokens\\n                best_indices = indices\\n        return {'selected_indices': list(best_indices), 'tokens_used': best_tokens, 'total_score': best_score}\\n\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement `solve(case)` that takes a payload with `lengths`, `scores`, `budget`, and optionally `_case_nonce`. The task is a budgeted sentence selection: we have sentences with lengths (token count) and scores (salience). We need to select a subset of sentences (by index) such that total length <= budget, maximize sum of scores, preserve document order (i.e., the order of indices as they appear in the input). The output must include `selected_indices` (list of integers, 0-based indices), `tokens_used` (integer), `total_score` (float). The algorithm should handle ties: break ties by fewer used tokens, then lexicographic source